OL,3,GNEWSARestored wetland becomes haven for
OL,4,Arare birds
OL,5,
OL,6,FA restored wetland in Cheshire is now
OL,7,Fhome to almost two-thirds of the UK's
OL,8,Fbreeding black-necked grebes, one of
OL,9,Fthe country's rarest breeding birds.
OL,11,FWoolston Eyes, near Warrington, was
OL,12,Fpreviously a dumping ground for
OL,13,Fdredging from the Manchester Ship
OL,14,FCanal. It is now the site of the
OL,15,Fcountry's largest colony of the
OL,16,Fspecies.
OL,18,FBlack-necked grebes are known for their
OL,19,Fdistinctive golden facial tufts and
OL,20,Faverage about 55 breeding pairs in the
OL,21,FUK each year, according to the RSPB.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
